rows={
982:r('POST inventory/count-adjustments calls RecordCountAdjustmentHandler with unchanged request. Same inventory-count-RequestId replays movement before validation. Otherwise direction parses enum, quantity positive/reason required, actor/item must exist and selected actor inventory_manage or approval authorizes. It inserts signed CountAdjustment movement plus audit in single SaveChanges, with no balance recomputation or source-funds check: direction/quantity are explicitly human-observed correction, not absolute new physical count. Negative resulting book stock is not forbidden. Unique movement key backs same-request race recovery.',
 'RequestId,InventoryItemId,Direction,QuantityMilliUnits,Reason,ActorUserId,approval IDs.', '200 RecordCountAdjustmentResult(MovementId,ItemId,WasReplayed);409 InventoryConflict;422 shape/authority;404 actor/item.', 'Appends stock correction and audit only; no Treasury/financial journal/order/print writes.', 'SEC001 actor sink. Observed quantity/direction trusted after inventory authority; no physical sensor or count verification.', 'StockMovementHandlers32-84 replay/entity reads; SaveChanges73 automatically transacts movement+audit; DbUpdate rereads key then409. No item quantity lock because additive observed correction.', 'Counts are delta movements, not SetBalance command; UI should not send observed absolute shelf count as delta.', 'Small ID reads and append; no full movement history query.', 'Same-key replay ignores changed item/direction/amount and returns original item; distinct keys intentionally both append. Enum.TryParse numeric values lack IsDefined check locally.', ['User-observed additive correction must remain clear','SEC001 sink; no payload-bound replay','Numeric undefined enum candidate if accepted by DB'], ['Same-key lost response/race, signed In/Out, absolute-versus-delta UI contract, zero quantity, numeric direction and rollback audit atomicity'], ['Program.cs982-1001 -> RecordCountAdjustmentHandler.HandleAsync','Infrastructure/Inventory/StockMovementHandlers.cs32-84','Domain/Inventory/InventoryRules.cs27-31 AssertCountAdjustmentInput']),
1003:r('POST inventory/waste invokes RecordWasteHandler. inventory-waste-RequestId replay first; loss type must parse and belong Waste/Spoilage/Breakage, positive quantity/reason required, actor/item exist and inventory_manage/approval authorizes. It reads last actual priced PurchaseReceipt, freezes unit cost and loss value or null, then appends Out stock movement and audit; large quantity>=10000milliUnits gives critical severity. Estimated/prep computed costs are deliberately not substituted for missing purchase cost. It does not prohibit loss exceeding current stock or post Treasury expense.',
 'RequestId,InventoryItemId,LossType,QuantityMilliUnits,Reason,ActorUserId,approval IDs.', '200 RecordWasteResult(MovementId,ItemId,UnitCost?,LossValue?,WasReplayed);409 conflict;422 invalid loss/quantity/reason/authority;404 actor/item.', 'Out loss stock movement and audit in single SaveChanges; no cash payment or printer.', 'SEC001 actor sink; observed loss quantity trusted, not proof shelf state. Real approval token separately checked.', 'StockMovementHandlers113-189 actor/item/approval and priced purchase reads then SaveChanges; DbUpdate replay by unique key. Purchase cost observation not locked against newer invoice.', 'Loss category remains distinct operational reason; unknown historical value null stays frozen even if later invoice arrives.', 'Loads all priced purchase receipts for item to choose latest rather than TOP1; history cost scales.', 'Same key prevents duplicate loss on retry but payload not compared; current source read can differ across distinct losses, by design.', ['Unknown-cost loss counted but value omitted in loss summary','No estimated/prep valuation substitution','SEC001 authority'], ['No purchase cost null, later purchase does not restate loss, three types only, critical threshold, negative resulting stock allowed, replay one movement/audit'], ['Program.cs1003-1022 -> RecordWasteHandler.HandleAsync','Infrastructure/Inventory/StockMovementHandlers.cs113-189','Domain/Inventory/InventoryRules.cs33-38 AssertWasteInput','Domain/Inventory/PurchasingRules.cs LastPurchaseUnitCost/ValueStockLoss']),
1024:r('POST recipes calls SaveRecipeHandler. It validates name/product ID/positive line quantities and rejects active empty recipe, then actor menu_manage/approval. In transaction it upserts explicit RecipeId or recipe-RequestId, replaces full ingredient set and updates selected product.RecipeId when active or clears if it currently references this inactive recipe. Product missing does not explicitly throw; raw line Kind/yield and ingredient references not comprehensively validated here. Reassigning existing recipe from productA toB does not clear old A link in this method, a concrete possible cause of divergent sibling recipe/price resolution; requires independent challenge.',
 'RequestId,RecipeId?,ProductId,Name,Active,Lines(ingredient,quantity,Kind,yield),ActorUserId,approval IDs.', '200 RecipeDto;422 shape/authority/active-empty;404 actor;persisted reference/enum failures500.', 'Transaction replaces recipe lines/header and optional selected product backlink; no immediate stock usage or cash/print.', 'SEC001 selected actor sink; product/ingredient/line semantic input persists under menu authority. Current old product reference not cleared when changing parent.', 'SaveRecipeHandler31-110 includes recipe graph, removes old lines/adds replacements, product read, SaveChanges/Commit. No optimistic version or row lock against concurrent edits.', 'Active recipe backlink makes future checkout/report current-recipe mapping work; historic orders are not versioned and therefore theoretical historical reports can change.', 'Graph replace proportional to line count; one transaction, no per-ingredient cost queries.', 'Stable ID upsert, not immutable replay: repeating old request after newer edit can overwrite. Concurrent same-ID creates may fail DB500.', ['Old product backlink retained on recipe ProductId change candidate','Unvalidated Kind can later Enum.Parse fail costing','Concurrent/stale full replacement'], ['Move recipe A->B backlink checks, deactivate matching link only, active empty blocked, malformed yield/kind/reference, concurrent replacement and no stock effect'], ['Program.cs1024-1039 -> SaveRecipeHandler.HandleAsync','Infrastructure/Inventory/SaveRecipeHandler.cs31-110','Infrastructure/Inventory/InventoryQueryService.cs price resolution and ToDomainLine']),
1138:r('POST customers/upsert calls UpsertCustomerHandler without caller actor or dedicated permission, intentionally ordinary order-taking. CustomerRules validates phone/name and normalizes phone, then phase1 find-or-create uses unique Phone constraint with race fallback. Separate transaction update-locks customer and address set, updates name and merges matching address when both Area/Street nonblank; otherwise no address change. Full addresses reread after commit and returned. First new customer SaveChanges occurs before merge transaction, so later failure can leave newly created bare customer; name is last writer wins, address rows merged safely under lock.',
 'Phone,Name,optional Area/Street/Building/Floor/Apartment/Landmark/ServiceId/ServiceName; cancellation; no actor or RequestId.', '200 CustomerDto(all saved addresses);422 CustomerRules domain only caught; missing/race/SQL failures500.', 'Creates/updates customer and address PII; no Order,checkout,charge,stock or print. Existing order customer snapshots not rewritten here.', 'Authenticated order taker can update any normalized known phone; no owner token, customer verification or claimed actor. Service name/id stored from request not catalog-validated locally.', 'UpsertCustomerHandler23-111 phase1 creation commit then phase2 transaction with customer/address UPDLOCK HOLDLOCK; second save/commit, then independent final-address read.', 'Shared Cashier/CallCenter address book; Area or Street missing silently means no address merge, not failure. Returned data is real persisted contacts.', 'Phone unique lookup, lock per customer, address materialization and final list; no N+1 address queries.', 'No request replay receipt; content address matching limits duplicates but repeated requests refresh name/time. Unrelated DbUpdate catch during phase1 assumes winning same-phone row and FirstAsync may throw.', ['Partial customer creation if address merge fails','Last-writer name and caller-supplied service metadata','All contacts for known phone under session-only order-taking policy'], ['Phone normalization collision, concurrent same/new addresses, incomplete Area/Street, failed phase2 leaves phase1 row, changed name, service mismatch'], ['Program.cs1138-1149 -> UpsertCustomerHandler.HandleAsync','Infrastructure/Customers/UpsertCustomerHandler.cs23-125','Domain/Customers/CustomerRules.cs AssertUpsertInput/NormalizePhone/FindMatchingAddress'])
}
